    "text": "A train moves towards a stationary observer with speed <math><mn>34</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></math> The train sounds a whistle and its frequency registered by the observer is <math><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> If the speed of the train is reduced to <math><mn>17</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></math> the frequency registered is <math><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> If speed of sound is <math><mn>340</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></math> then the ratio <math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></math> is:",
